    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Welcome to No. 18 Corn Mill, a wonderful top (second) floor 1 bedroom apartment boasting a sunny facing balcony with views across the City, very generous accommodation, ready to walk into and the benefit of a designated underground car parking space. \r\n\r\nO'Connor Estate Agents are delighted to present this stunning bright property to the market which presents itself in pristine condition. The apartment extends to approx. 45sq.m. (484sq.ft.) and offers generous bright living space, ample storage and a large double bedroom. There is also access to a large Residents Roof Top Garden with amazing vistas of Croke Park and the City.    \r\n\r\nThe accommodation briefly comprises of a large Entrance Hall with ample storage, a bright open plan living / dining room with a large sunny balcony and adjoining a modern built-in kitchen. The Bedroom is a large double with built in wardrobes and a main bathroom. \r\n\r\nThe Corn Mill development is ideally situated within walking distance from the City Centre and Drumcondra village is a short stroll away offering an abundance of shops, bars, cafes and restaurants. The development is located just minutes from Croke Park.\r\n\r\n**TRANSPORT** - Drumcondra Train Station is only a few minutes walk away and Clontarf Dart Station is also within easy reach. There are numerous bus routes in the immediate locality, Dublin City Centre is within walking distance and the M50 and M1 are easily accessible offering excellent transport links to the rest of the county and country. Dublin Airport is also within close proximity.\r\n\r\n**AMENITIES** - Conveniently located off Clonliffe Road there are a number of shops, bars and restaurants in the busy thoroughfare of Drumcondra and Fairview. For the sports enthusiast, Croke Park is your neighbour and there are numerous gyms, football clubs and sports grounds nearby.\r\n\r\nViewing is Highly Recommended.\r\n\r\nPLANS MAY NOT BE TO SCALE AND ARE FOR ILLUSTRATION PURPOSES ONLY"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation comprises:\r\nHallway: with wooden flooring, audio intercom and access to walk-in storage. \r\nLiving / Dining Room: c.4.62m x 3.8m with wooden floors, extensive glazing and access to private balcony. \r\nKitchen: c. 2.4m x 2.51 with tiled floors and part tiled walls and modern build in press units.  \r\nBedroom: c.4.01m x 3.01m with wooden flooring and built in wardrobes.\r\nBathroom: c.2.06m x c.1.69m with floor and part wall tiling with WC, WHB and Bath."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Superb Top (Second) Floor One Bedroom Apartment\r\nDesignated Underground Car Space\r\nSunny Private Balcony \r\nAccess to Residents Roof Top Garden with views across Croke Park and the City\r\nAnnual Service Charge €1,555\r\nOnly a few minutes walk to bustling Drumcondra & Fairview Villages\r\nWalking distance to Dublin City Centre\r\nExcellent transport links including Drumcondra Train & Clontarf Dart Stations\r\nNo Rental Cap\r\nOn view by Appointment"
